life-science biosensor diagnostics  incorporated a member of the IQ group  global presents the saliva glucose  biosensor diabetes is recognized as the  world's fastest-growing chronic disease  one in 11 people has diabetes  that's 415 million people every six  seconds a person dies from diabetes five  hundred and forty two thousand children  have type 1 diabetes 12 percent of  global health expenditure is spent on  diabetes six hundred and seventy three  billion u.s. dollars the global market  for glucose monitoring devices is  expected to grow from 10 billion u.s.  dollars in 2015 to twelve point four  billion u.s. dollars in 2020 by 2040 it  is estimated one in ten will have  diabetes that's six hundred and forty  two million people diabetes related  health expenditure will exceed eight  hundred and two billion US dollars blood  glucose monitoring is essential when  managing diabetes it helps patients  understand the link between blood  glucose food exercise and their diabetes  medication  affective diabetes monitoring relies on  obtaining numerous daily blood samples  from finger pricks that are invasive  painful and inconvenient patients  families and doctors want a monitoring  system that is non-invasive pain-free  quick and reliable introducing the novel  saliva glucose biosensor system what is  a biosensor  a device that monitors and transmits  information about a biological process  the glucose biosensor consists of an  organic thin film transistor which  integrates glucose oxidase and reacts  with salivary glucose resulting in  hydrogen peroxide which is decomposed  into proton ions generating an  electrical signal this signal is then  processed by a smart device the glucose  biosensor measures glucose in saliva  enabling mobile monitoring that is pain  free quick and accurate the technology  offers patients caregivers and  healthcare professionals the ability to  track store and share health data  revolutionising diabetes care what  starts here changes the world
 

